Provenance notices
------------------
* Pool D of this system was produced by RUNNING the upstream DeepEye-SQL
  pipeline (https://github.com/HKUSTDial/DeepEye-SQL, MIT License,
  "Copyright (c) 2026 DeepEye-SQL Team") pinned to commit
  252ab45a7adf9f88fb93d1ff27ca019d20f0449a, with the following documented
  adaptations that touch plumbing only, not the algorithm:
    1. LLM backend swapped to a different OpenAI-compatible model served
       through an internal gateway (generation config per our model policy).
    2. Embedding stage pointed at a gateway embedding API instead of the
       local default model.
    3. Device: cuda -> cpu (no GPU available on the host).
    4. Sampling strategy: gateway rejects n>1 per request, so each sample
       is sent as an independent 1-sample request (identical prompt and
       temperature; only server-side batching semantics changed).
    5. One-line robustness patch upstream: llm.ask(..., timeout=600).
    6. Dependency lock adjustments for the offline environment.
  Schema linking, value retrieval, generation templates and DeepEye's own
  answer selection are used exactly as published. Upstream code is NOT
  redistributed in this repository: reproduce by cloning upstream at the
  pinned commit and applying the config-level adaptations above.
